description:
Adds up to 40 books to the reader's ReadingRate library in one call, by ReadingRate book id, all on the same shelf (want-to-read unless a status is given). Books already in the library are left where they are and listed.

Use after lookup_books_batch has matched a photographed shelf or a list, and the reader has said which of the matched books to add. Books added as read also go on the reader's ReadingRate activity feed; other readers see that they finished them while the reader's profile is public and shows finished books (new accounts start private, and finished books start hidden). It takes ids only, so it never adds a book to the catalog; a book lookup_books_batch could not match is added with add_book_to_library once the reader confirms its title.

Example: {"book_ids": ["<book id>", "<book id>"], "status": "read"}
